# Keeping the build context small is not cosmetic: everything here would
# otherwise be uploaded to the daemon on every build, and bin/obj from a Windows
# host would collide with the Linux build inside the image.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
**/publish/

.git/
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/

# Generated code-graph artifact — large, and rebuilt by `graphify update .`
graphify-out/

**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Local state that must never bake into an image.
# These are spelled out rather than globbed: `**/Logs/` also matches the source
# folder Application/Features/Commands/Logs, which silently broke the build.
# Neither Dockerfile actually COPYs the repo root broadly enough to reach .env
# (each names specific files/dirs one at a time — see src/cms/.../Dockerfile and
# src/web/.../Dockerfile), so this is defense-in-depth against a future Dockerfile
# change, not a fix for a live leak — but keeping .env out of the build context
# is still the correct default.
**/appsettings.Development.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
src/cms/Presentation/Wasm/Wasm/wwwroot/uploads/
src/cms/Presentation/Wasm/Wasm/Logs/
src/cms/Presentation/Wasm/Wasm/Backups/
src/web/Presentation/WebMvc/Logs/
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
